            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery aneurysm following drug-coated balloon treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>505-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.carrev.2015.08.001</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1553-8389(15)00194-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Drug-coated balloons are an effective treatment option for stent restenosis. Because of their potential benefits, the use of drug-coated balloons is predicted to increase in the future and expand further for the treatment of de novo lesions as well. We hereby present a case in which a patient developed a coronary artery aneurysm following the treatment of a de novo native coronary narrowing with a drug-coated balloon.</AbstractText>
